1
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,780
Hi, I'm Nada.

2
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:09,059
I'm a diabeticologist,

3
00:00:09,059 --> 00:00:09,800
and I want to talk

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,890
to you today about diabetes.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,380
Diabetes is a very common

6
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:14,830
disease worldwide,

7
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:15,760
and it's good to know

8
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,590
some information about it.

9
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:18,120
What is

10
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,320
diabetes? Diabetes means

11
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,990
increase in the blood sugar,

12
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,340
and it could be due

13
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:23,930
to

14
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,240
problem in the insulin

15
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:26,670
secretion from the body,

16
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,000
or it could be due

17
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,880
to insulin resistance.

18
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,280
There are some symptoms that

19
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:32,250
if you have,

20
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:33,300
you have to check your

21
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,640
blood sugar to exclude if

22
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,030
you have diabetes.

23
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,820
These symptoms include

24
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:38,550
fatigue,

25
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,010
blurring of vision,

26
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,920
and increase the frequency of

27
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:42,850
urination,

28
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,070
increase the sense of thirst.

29
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:47,570
Unexplained weight loss also

30
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:49,940
is a very significant symptom.

31
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:50,980
There are two types of

32
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:51,860
diabetes,

33
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:52,660
type one,

34
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,000
which is usually common in

35
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,070
younger age,

36
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,840
and it happens because of

37
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:58,650
lack of insulin secretion,

38
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,440
and type two diabetes,

39
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:02,610
which is because of insulin

40
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,920
resistance and it's common as

41
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:06,380
like a familial disease that

42
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,500
runs in families.

43
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,420
Diabetes is a chronic disease,

44
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:10,700
that's why it's associated

45
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:11,160
with many

46
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,310
complications.

47
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:13,740
It may affect the eye,

48
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:14,800
causing something called

49
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,310
diabetic retinopathy,

50
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,180
and it also may affect

51
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,920
the nerves in the extremities,

52
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:21,160
like the legs and the

53
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:23,460
hands, causing numbness and

54
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,110
pin-needle sensation.

55
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:26,520
It could also affect the

56
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:27,410
kidneys,

57
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,280
and also it could affect

58
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:29,820
the heart,

59
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:31,160
making this patient more

60
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,280
liable for heart attacks and

61
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,240
more liable for

62
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:35,110
strokes.

63
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:36,840
That's why diabetes is

64
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,520
considered as an invisible

65
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,880
disability. There are some

66
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:41,340
advices that I usually give

67
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:42,280
to my patients,

68
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,030
especially who do long shifts.

69
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:46,110
Please keep yourself hydrated.

70
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:47,540
Don't miss your meals.

71
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:48,840
Take your meals- and take

72
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:49,790
your snacks.

73
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:51,580
And please do have good

74
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:52,840
choices for the food and

75
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:54,330
avoid any junk food.

76
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,480
And if you are feeling

77
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,860
tired or unwell,

78
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,960
please check your blood

79
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,360
glucose. And if you have

80
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:00,650
hypoglycemia,

81
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:02,140
don't leave yourself like

82
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,590
this. Try to take,

83
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:04,310
um,

84
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:05,780
some juice or some,

85
00:02:05,780 --> 00:02:06,940
like, sugar tablets or

86
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:07,710
whatever,

87
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:09,140
and check your blood glucose

88
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:10,640
and make sure that it's

89
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:12,480
not hypoglycemic anymore.

90
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:13,479
And for everyone,

91
00:02:13,479 --> 00:02:14,400
if you notice one of

92
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,560
your colleagues who looks

93
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,400
unwell, please check his blood

94
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,740
sugar as soon as possible.

95
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:20,240
And if there's no glucometer

96
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,900
around, then give him a

97
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:24,050
sugary drink or some juice

98
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:26,310
because hypoglycemia is fatal,

99
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:27,340
so we have to prevent

100
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:29,690
hypoglycemia as we can.

101
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,100
Diabetes is not a stigma,

102
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,140
so please support your

103
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:34,260
colleagues who are living with

104
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,950
diabetes. Thank you.
